@page "/components/lists"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Lists

<DocsHeader Title="Lists" Eyebrow="Components">
    <Lead>Rows with a title, a description, a status badge and content at the start or end. A row can be a link or a button.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<h2 id="item">A single row</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(SingleItem)">
    <p>On its own, a <code>StilListItem</code> is a bordered box. <code>Badge</code> is a shortcut for a status badge at the end of the row; set its color with <code>BadgeVariant</code>.</p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="list">A list of links</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(OrderList)">
    <p>Inside a <code>StilList</code> the rows are joined. A row with <code>Href</code> is a link, so the whole row can be clicked and opened in a new tab. Links work without interactivity.</p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="start-end">Start and end content</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(StartAndEnd)">
    <p><code>Start</code> holds an avatar or an icon before the title. <code>End</code> holds buttons or a menu after the badge. Do not put buttons in a row that is itself a link or a button; nested controls are hard to use with a keyboard or screen reader.</p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="selection">Clickable rows</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Selectable)">
    <p>A row with <code>OnClick</code> is a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>, so it can be focused and pressed with Enter or Space. <code>Selected</code> marks the current row with <code>aria-current</code>, and <code>Disabled</code> turns it off. Clicks need an interactive render mode.</p>
</DocExample>

<p>For a list inside a card, see <a href="components/cards#card-content">Lists and tables in a card</a>.</p>

